# Frontend Environment Variables (.env)
# The frontend uses Vite, so to expose an environment variable it needs to be prefixed with 'VITE_'.
# 
# For local development, VITE_API_BASE_URL should not be strictly necessary since vite proxy uses /api.
# However, if running the backend separately without vite proxy (e.g for production split testing), configure this:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000/api

# For PRODUCTION on Vercel/Netlify, set this explicitly in the platform's Environment Variables panel 
# to the Render Backend URL for all API calls:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend-app-name.onrender.com/api
